9front's libdraw (the client side: initdraw, the draw protocol, fonts,
event), copied from the Plan2001 CPU server's 9front (1.10.2026; 9front is
MIT-licensed; not warptest.c and test.c, tests), for Plan 9 programs built as WebAssembly on drawterm's
kernel in the browser (../../wasmapp).  Not here: what drawterm's own
libdraw has the same (arith badrect bytesperline chan defont drawrepl fmt
icossin icossin2 mkwarp rectclip rgb); alloc.c and warp.c are here
although drawterm has them: they use the Display and Image, and 9front's
Display is not drawterm's (usrlock), so drawterm's would misread it.
Changed here: stringbg.c - its op parameters Drawop, not int (Plan 9's C
takes an enum for an int, clang does not); event.c - its slaves (mouse, keyboard, timer, estart) are
kprocs, not forked processes: there is no fork; no notes either.
